Description: pvr: count buffer slices of compressed copies in blocks
 Buffer to image and image to buffer copies use an uncompressed copy format
 with the block size of the compressed image (pvr_get_raw_copy_format()).
 The distance between two slices or array layers in the buffer was computed
 from the row length and image height in texels times that block size. For
 an ETC2 RGB8 image of 64x64 texels that is 64 * 64 * 8 = 32768 bytes instead
 of 16 * 16 * 8 = 2048 bytes, so every layer after the first of a region was
 read from or written to the wrong place in the buffer. The buffer to image
 path did have a conversion to blocks, but it tested the copy format, which
 is never compressed, and would have multiplied by the block size twice.
 The row stride itself was already right: pvr_setup_buffer_surface() takes
 it in texels and divides by the block width.
 .
 Convert the row length and image height to blocks of the image format
 before computing the slice size, in both directions. Uncompressed formats
 are unchanged.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
